    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69571" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶλυς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υ</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>soft, weak, feeble</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ.
				ἐπιστείβων</span>, of a serpent, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				32
			</span></i>, cf. Sch. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			metaph., <i>weak in intellect, dull</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
			</span></i> Lac.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1014.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (who also has 
				Comp.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				693
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μωλύτερον φαίνεσθαι τὸν λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Socr.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					30.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶλυς ῥίζα,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶλυ</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				679
			</span></i>.</div>
